<Sec id="t-voice" n="7" title="Your duties when you deploy voice" short="Tell people they are talking to AI, get consent before you record, and follow the laws where your users are.">
  <p>When you use the Services to talk to your own users, you are responsible for how you deploy them. In particular, you will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell your users, clearly and before or at the start of a conversation, that they are speaking with an AI system and not a person, where the law requires it or where a reasonable person could be misled;</li>
    <li>give your users any privacy notice the law requires, and obtain every consent needed to process their voice and other data, including consent from all parties to record a conversation where the law requires it;</li>
    <li>have a lawful basis for all processing you instruct us to carry out, and comply with the DPA;</li>
    <li>not present a character, voice or agent as a real, identifiable person without that person's written permission;</li>
    <li>keep a way for users to reach a human or another channel where your use case calls for one;</li>
    <li>follow the laws that apply to your use, including laws on consumer protection, telemarketing, recording, AI disclosure, accessibility and data protection.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The Services are not designed for, and must not be used for, calls to emergency services or as the only channel for safety-critical communication.</p>
