<Sec id="t-ai" n="9" title="AI output, characters and your brain" short="AI output, including transcripts and replies, can be wrong. You are responsible for what your brain or agent says, and a person should make any decision that seriously affects someone.">
  <p>The Services use machine learning to transcribe speech, generate speech, animate characters and, in Plug &amp; Play, generate replies. Their output may be inaccurate, incomplete or inappropriate. Transcripts may contain errors, and a generated reply may state things that are not true. Output is not professional, legal, medical or financial advice.</p>
  <p>In developer integration, your brain decides what the agent says and does, and you are responsible for it. In Plug &amp; Play, you are responsible for the instructions, knowledge and tools you configure and for reviewing how the agent behaves before you deploy it.</p>
  <p>You must not use output from the Services as the sole basis for any decision that has legal or similarly significant effects on a person, such as decisions about credit, employment, insurance, healthcare or access to services. Use independent human judgment and consider other factors.</p>
  <p>We work to reduce errors and bias in our systems, and we review and update them regularly, but we do not warrant that they are free of errors or bias.</p>
